course: dictionary
lesson: 11054
title: Weedkiller: a dangerous word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A weedkiller is a chemical that kills weeds, the unwanted wild plants that grow in gardens, on paths and in fields. Look at the two parts of the word: weed plus killer. The second part tells you what it does.
explain: «A boy in Leeds drank from a juice bottle in the shed that held weedkiller.» The sentence says he was very ill and his throat was burnt. Those clues show that weedkiller is poison, not a drink.
explain: Context helps you work out meaning, but it also warns you about safety. When a word is linked to harm, stop, do not touch it, and tell an adult.
fact: Weedkiller is a chemical that kills weeds.
fact: Weeds are unwanted wild plants that grow in gardens, on paths and in fields.
fact: Weedkiller is poisonous, so it must be kept locked away, out of reach of children and pets.
fact: Only adults should use weedkiller.
fact: Some weedkillers can harm insects and wildlife, so some gardeners pull weeds out by hand instead.
exercise: What is weedkiller? | A tasty drink for the garden | *A chemical that kills unwanted wild plants | A tool for cutting the grass | A plant that grows wild in fields
exercise: «A boy in Leeds drank from a juice bottle in the shed that held weedkiller.» What do the clues tell you about weedkiller? | It is good for children to play with | It is safe to drink if it is in a juice bottle | *Keep it locked away, because it is poisonous
exercise: Some gardeners pull weeds out by hand. Why might they do that? | Weeds like being pulled out | Hands are better at spraying than bottles | Weedkiller makes weeds grow faster | *Some weedkillers can harm insects and wildlife
test: Which word means the wild plants that grow where they are not wanted? | grass | *weeds | seeds | flowers
test: Who should use weedkiller? | pets | children | *adults only | everyone at school
exam: What should you do if you find a bottle of weedkiller somewhere it should not be? | Pour it on the grass to see what happens | *Tell an adult straight away and keep everyone away from it | Leave it near the children's toys | Drink a little to see what it tastes like
